cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UV-Vis Spectrum Studio in research, please cite the exact software release used. After Zenodo archives a release, prefer the DOI for that archived version."
title: "UV-Vis Spectrum Studio"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hasan
    given-names: Abdulsalam S.
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abd19990044-commits/uv-vis-spectrum-studio"
url: "https://github.com/abd19990044-commits/uv-vis-spectrum-studio"
abstract: >-
  UV-Vis Spectrum Studio is an open-source, cross-platform scientific environment
  for UV-Vis spectral processing, publication-quality visualization, quantitative
  analysis, analytical-method validation, multicomponent spectrophotometry,
  derivative spectroscopy, peak fitting and deconvolution, Fourier/wavelet
  analysis, chemometrics, and reproducible tamper-evident project files.
keywords:
  - UV-Vis spectroscopy
  - analytical chemistry
  - spectrophotometry
  - chemometrics
  - analytical method validation
  - derivative spectrophotometry
  - peak deconvolution
  - multicomponent analysis
  - reproducible research
  - scientific software
